![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `loadDatabaseAuthoritativeProfile` function currently returns `null` on any database query error. This masks actual database connection or system errors as simple authentication failures (e.g., 'Invalid token' 401). Instead, it should explicitly check for the expected 'no rows found' error code (`PGRST116`) and propagate any other unexpected database errors so they can be handled as 500 Internal Server Errors.

```javascript
async function loadDatabaseAuthoritativeProfile(userId) {
  const client = getServiceClient();
  const { data, error } = await client
    .from('user_profiles')
    .select('id, email, role, status')
    .eq('id', userId)
    .single();

  if (error) {
    if (error.code === 'PGRST116') {
      return null;
    }
    throw error;
  }

  if (!data || (data.status && data.status !== 'active')) {
    return null;
  }

  return data;
}
```

